            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An apparatus for measuring a jugular vein pressure waveform comprises a rotation sensor (102) configured to produce a measurement signal when being against a skin of an individual and in a movement sensing relation with a jugular vein (104) of the individual. The apparatus comprises a processing system (101) configured to receive the measurement signal and produce a waveform of a motion of the skin in a direction perpendicular to the skin based on the measurement signal indicative of rotation of the rotation sensor, where the waveform of the motion of the skin is indicative of the jugular vein pressure waveform. The rotation sensor that measures rotation is more insensitive to movements not related to variation of the jugular vein pressure than for example an acceleration sensor.</p>
            </abstract>
